    "result_text": "All 263 tests pass with a clean build. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: structured address form\n\nThe request now accepts a structured address (`addressLine1`, optional `addressLine2`, `city`, `postcode`) while remaining backward-compatible with the flat `address` input.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` to the `OwnerFields` schema (so they appear on both request and response DTOs), documented the composed-`address` behavior, and removed `address` from the `required` list so structured-only owners pass bean validation. `addressLine1` is intentionally left with no `minLength`/non-blank pattern so a blank value can fall back to the flat `address` in controller logic rather than being rejected up front.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added persisted `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` fields (columns `address_line1`/`address_line2`) with accessors, and dropped `@NotEmpty` from `address` since it is now optional at the contract level.\n\n**Schema files** (`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the two new columns; the JPA-backed test profile (`hsqldb`, `ddl-auto=none`) needs them to exist. Also relaxed `address NOT NULL` in the h2 schema.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner` (and mirrored in `updateOwner`):\n- Prefer the structured fields when a non-blank `addressLine1` is supplied; otherwise use the flat `address`.\n- Normalization (`normaliseAddress`) applies to whichever fields are supplied.\n- An owner is valid when it has an address in either form plus city; otherwise `400`.\n- The stored/returned `address` is the normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space and normalized `addressLine2` appended when present.\n\nThe household hash, postcode validation, and locality all read `postcode`/`city` \u2014 single top-level fields shared by both address forms \u2014 so they already resolve correctly regardless of which form is used; the composed value is stored in `owner.getAddress()` for anything downstream that reads it.\n\nThe acceptance test confirms structured input `\"10 king st\"` returns `addressLine1` = `\"10 KING STREET\"` and `address` = `\"10 KING STREET\"`, and the flat-address path still succeeds.",
